# Assistant memory files

Development-assistant memory lives in `memory/*.md`. Retrieval over those files **is** the memory RAG. It is a separate corpus from SkillSet / ESCO / pgvector / Ollama skill RAG. Never query skill embeddings to answer assistant-memory questions.

## Retrieve (RAG)

For the current user request:

1. Read `memory/MEMORY.md` (the index).
2. Search `memory/` (filenames, titles, summaries) and open only the files that match this task.
3. Prefer a few relevant files over dumping every memory into context.

Manual trigger: `@memory` or “用 memory RAG 查 …”.

## When to write

Create or update a short file under `memory/` when the user corrects a **project rule** or a **repeated writing/workflow habit**. Same class of mistake a second time should already be on disk.

Do not dump `AGENTS.md` architecture into memory. Do not write secrets, tokens, or credentials—environment variable **names** are OK.

## How to name files

`memory/{prefix}_{kebab-case-slug}.md`

- `project_` — product/architecture hard rules
- `feedback_` — corrected implementation or process
- `reference_` — lookup facts (paths, env var names, UI behavior)
- `user_` — personal preferences (gitignored)

Keep each file about 5–15 lines. After writing, add one index line to `memory/MEMORY.md`: title, one-sentence summary, filename link.

Do not paste memory contents into this rule.
